  CISA ADVISORY — ICS-CERT ALERT (SAMPLE)
  AA26-045A: Critical Windows Server Vulnerability
====================================================================

Release Date:       February 14, 2026
Source:             Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA)
Classification:     TLP:CLEAR
CVE:                CVE-2026-21001
CVSS Score:         9.8 (Critical)
Affected Products:  Windows Server 2019, 2022, 2025
Vendor:             Microsoft Corporation

SUMMARY:
---------
A critical remote code execution vulnerability exists in the Windows
Server Message Block (SMB) service. An unauthenticated attacker could
send specially crafted packets to a vulnerable SMB server to achieve
code execution with SYSTEM privileges.

IMPACT:
-------
Successful exploitation allows:
- Remote code execution without authentication
- Complete system compromise
- Lateral movement across domain-joined systems
- Potential domain-wide compromise

MITIGATION:
-----------
- Apply Microsoft security update KB5035849 immediately
- Disable SMBv1 if not already disabled
- Block TCP port 445 at network perimeter
- Enable Windows Firewall rules restricting SMB access

AFFECTED ACS SYSTEMS:
---------------------
{{ prefix }}-ACS-SRV-002 — File Server (Windows Server 2022)
{{ prefix }}-Legacy_Server — Application Server (Windows Server 2016)

